      "reader": "Selected action (reading only):\npatch the field work rig (2 measures)\n\nYou see a field work rig.\nThe clay working surface has split. Its fittings cannot hold a weapon steady. Release the rig before patching or using it.\nRepair: 2 measures of fire clay or prepared lining clay, in any mix. Composition: Masonry.\nCold work here: dismantle tool (from a released extraction tool); make cargo sled (from a iron spike); make discharge rod (from a iron spike); make hand bellows (from a iron spike); make hand pump (from a iron spike); make hand sieve (from a iron spike); make hearth nozzle (from a iron spike); make steam condenser (from a iron spike); dress iron point (from a recovered iron blank); reclaim iron and timber (from a released extraction tool). Carry the find in your pack and stand beside it.\n\nA clay-faced work surface rests on two sound timber braces. A weathered plate reads: \"Left for whoever can use it.\" Restore its workshop services or dismantle it for two salvaged timber, permanently losing this rig. Repair clay is not recovered. It can be hauled locally. Across a straight area edge, align it behind you on plain, clear ground: preparation costs two hauling rounds before crossing. If interrupted, spent effort is not returned. Release it before working. Single weapons can still be assembled from carried components without a workshop.",
